0009-expose-search-state-changed-hook.patch

Two changes enabling all-match search highlighting from the host app:

1. TerminalViewSearch.swift — adds `findAllMatchPositions(_:options:limit:)`
   A public method returning match positions as [(row: Int, col: Int, size: Int)]
   tuples, exposing the data from the module-internal SearchResult type without
   crossing the module boundary.

2. MacTerminalView.swift — adds `searchStateDidChange(term:options:)`
   An `open` callback that fires whenever the find bar's search term or options
   change, or the find bar is dismissed. Called from handleFindBarSearchChanged,
   handleFindBarOptionsChanged, and hideFindBar. Also clears findBarTerm in
   hideFindBar so the callback receives "" on dismissal.

Together these give a TerminalView subclass everything it needs to maintain
a transparent overlay of all-match highlights: the callback says WHEN to update,
and findAllMatchPositions says WHERE the matches are.

Pattern: same as patches 0006/0007 — an `open` hook on existing behaviour.
